WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.183
Start with your phone and television on the same trusted Wi-Fi network.

00:00:05.183 --> 00:00:06.862
Turn the television on.

00:00:06.862 --> 00:00:09.563
GlintBeam is a product by AILoopLabs.

00:00:09.563 --> 00:00:12.483
This guide uses labeled example TV data.

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:17.462
Read the first-use tips and select Next Tip to continue.

00:00:17.462 --> 00:00:24.247
These screenshots show example interface states, not a recording of a physical television responding.

00:00:24.247 --> 00:00:27.069
Supported controls depend on the TV model.

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:31.969
GlintBeam offers a directional pad and a swipe touchpad.

00:00:31.969 --> 00:00:34.328
The setup tips introduce both modes.

00:00:34.328 --> 00:00:40.683
Later, you can switch between them on the Remote screen and use whichever feels more comfortable.

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:47.852
The next tip introduces TV app shortcuts, typed searches, and optional voice input.

00:00:47.852 --> 00:00:51.079
GlintBeam sends requests to your selected TV.

00:00:51.079 --> 00:00:56.673
Streaming services may require their own accounts, payments, or subscriptions.

00:00:57.900 --> 00:00:59.365
Choose Search for TVs.

00:00:59.365 --> 00:01:02.562
Keep the phone and TV on the same local network.

00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:05.426
You can revisit the previous tip with Back.

00:01:05.426 --> 00:01:09.621
The tutorial checkbox controls whether these tips appear again.

00:01:10.833 --> 00:01:16.935
If discovery finds nothing, confirm the TV is on and connected to the same Wi-Fi.

00:01:16.935 --> 00:01:18.215
Try Rescan Wi-Fi.

00:01:18.215 --> 00:01:24.241
Guest networks or network isolation can prevent devices from finding each other.

00:01:25.467 --> 00:01:30.960
Select your television from the discovered list, then use the blue pairing button.

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:32.434
Demo TV is an example.

00:01:32.434 --> 00:01:37.391
Confirm the name and brand belong to the television you intend to control.

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:42.796
If discovery misses your TV, use the manual connection section.

00:01:42.796 --> 00:01:47.591
Choose its brand and enter the TV address shown in its network settings.

00:01:47.591 --> 00:01:50.855
Do not enter an address copied from this example.

00:01:52.067 --> 00:01:57.025
Some TVs, including Samsung, show an approval request on the television.

00:01:57.025 --> 00:02:00.330
Allow GlintBeam there and wait for confirmation.

00:02:00.330 --> 00:02:06.045
This is an illustrated app state; your actual television prompt may look different.

00:02:07.267 --> 00:02:10.980
Other televisions request a PIN or configured key.

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:16.699
Enter the value from your television or its authorized settings, then verify.

00:02:16.699 --> 00:02:21.379
Never assume the sample code in a tutorial will pair a real TV.

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:26.418
If authorization fails, the pairing screen stays open.

00:02:26.418 --> 00:02:31.720
Check the TV, request a new prompt, or go back and select the device again.

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:35.325
A failed request does not mean the TV is connected.

00:02:36.533 --> 00:02:43.042
After the television confirms pairing, choose a recognizable name, such as Living Room TV.

00:02:43.042 --> 00:02:47.164
Assign a room so multiple televisions are easier to find.

00:02:47.164 --> 00:02:50.997
The saved profile remains in GlintBeam on this phone.

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:56.920
Choose Save and Open Remote after pairing and naming your television.

00:02:56.920 --> 00:02:59.315
The app then opens the main remote.

00:02:59.315 --> 00:03:05.951
The example shown here illustrates the destination; it is not evidence of hardware compatibility.

00:03:07.167 --> 00:03:11.923
Tap the directional arrows to move through the television interface.

00:03:11.923 --> 00:03:13.112
Tap OK to select.

00:03:13.112 --> 00:03:18.777
The top row includes power, source, the number pad, and keyboard or voice access.

00:03:18.777 --> 00:03:20.805
Check the TV for each result.

00:03:22.033 --> 00:03:23.566
Choose Swipe Touchpad.

00:03:23.566 --> 00:03:27.746
Swipe to navigate, tap to select, and double-tap to go back.

00:03:27.746 --> 00:03:36.037
These gestures send navigation requests; smooth pointer movement and other behavior depend on the selected TV protocol.

00:03:37.267 --> 00:03:44.688
Scroll down the remote to reach Back, Home, Movies, Guide, Menu, volume, mute, and channel controls.

00:03:44.688 --> 00:03:47.063
Some controls depend on your TV.

00:03:47.063 --> 00:03:52.406
Displayed information is not a continuously synchronized TV status feed.

00:03:53.633 --> 00:03:58.476
Use the bottom Movie Center tab for TV search and playback requests.

00:03:58.476 --> 00:04:02.749
Type a movie, show, or actor and send the search to your TV.

00:04:02.749 --> 00:04:07.379
GlintBeam does not supply movies or guarantee automatic playback.

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:12.569
Scroll within Movie Center to find app and input shortcuts.

00:04:12.569 --> 00:04:16.874
A request works only where the selected TV protocol supports it.

00:04:16.874 --> 00:04:23.063
An app tile does not include a streaming subscription or guarantee the service is installed.

00:04:24.267 --> 00:04:26.756
Input controls vary by television.

00:04:26.756 --> 00:04:32.758
Some models can select an input directly; others can only open the TV source menu.

00:04:32.758 --> 00:04:37.589
Check the actual TV screen and make any remaining selection there.

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:42.641
Open the microphone or keyboard button on the remote.

00:04:42.641 --> 00:04:45.902
Type a search or other TV text, then send it.

00:04:45.902 --> 00:04:53.221
Use ordinary non-sensitive text: some television control protocols use unencrypted local connections.

00:04:54.433 --> 00:04:56.123
Voice input is optional.

00:04:56.123 --> 00:04:59.643
Read the microphone explanation before continuing.

00:04:59.643 --> 00:05:04.008
Your Android speech provider may process audio on its servers.

00:05:04.008 --> 00:05:10.133
You can choose typed input instead; basic remote buttons do not need microphone access.

00:05:11.333 --> 00:05:15.193
The dial-pad button opens channel numbers and color keys.

00:05:15.193 --> 00:05:18.104
Use these only where your TV supports them.

00:05:18.104 --> 00:05:20.812
Close the sheet to return to the remote.

00:05:20.812 --> 00:05:25.145
Sending a number does not guarantee a particular channel exists.

00:05:26.367 --> 00:05:30.091
Open TVs and Setup to see saved devices and rooms.

00:05:30.091 --> 00:05:32.325
Select a TV to make it active.

00:05:32.325 --> 00:05:34.262
The heart marks favorites.

00:05:34.262 --> 00:05:40.146
Removing a TV deletes its saved profile and pairing credentials from GlintBeam.

00:05:41.367 --> 00:05:48.104
With more than one saved TV, use the top device selector or room filters to find the right one.

00:05:48.104 --> 00:05:54.344
Always check which TV is active before sending power, volume, search, or other commands.

00:05:55.567 --> 00:05:58.506
Choose Add TV to open the four-step wizard.

00:05:58.506 --> 00:06:02.061
Select the brand and read its preparation checklist.

00:06:02.061 --> 00:06:06.573
Prepare the television’s network-control settings before scanning.

00:06:06.573 --> 00:06:09.923
The wizard is separate from the initial tutorial.

00:06:11.133 --> 00:06:15.234
The wizard shows discovered devices for the selected brand.

00:06:15.234 --> 00:06:20.099
Select the intended television, or enter its network address manually.

00:06:20.099 --> 00:06:26.355
Example names and addresses shown in this guide must be replaced with your own TV details.

00:06:27.567 --> 00:06:32.045
Follow the authorization instructions for the selected television.

00:06:32.045 --> 00:06:35.031
Allow its prompt or enter its required code.

00:06:35.031 --> 00:06:38.084
Wait for a verified result before proceeding.

00:06:38.084 --> 00:06:41.817
Do not treat a pending handshake as successful pairing.

00:06:43.033 --> 00:06:49.555
In the compatibility step, try the displayed test buttons and check the television for the result.

00:06:49.555 --> 00:06:51.950
Name the device and assign its room.

00:06:51.950 --> 00:06:56.409
Only save once the app’s required verification steps are satisfied.

00:06:57.633 --> 00:07:03.655
The Brand Guide tab contains preparation instructions and protocol-specific information.

00:07:03.655 --> 00:07:05.366
Select your manufacturer.

00:07:05.366 --> 00:07:10.636
Use your television’s own settings and documentation where menu names differ.

00:07:10.636 --> 00:07:14.263
This guide does not certify every model from a brand.

00:07:15.467 --> 00:07:21.419
For LG, follow the TV’s registration or pairing prompt and wait for authorization.

00:07:21.419 --> 00:07:24.758
Features vary by model and supported protocol.

00:07:24.758 --> 00:07:31.146
A network connection alone is not proof that GlintBeam has permission to control the TV.

00:07:32.367 --> 00:07:39.796
Sony uses its separate IP Control path, with the TV’s PIN or configured pre-shared key where required.

00:07:39.796 --> 00:07:43.874
This is different from native Android TV remote pairing.

00:07:43.874 --> 00:07:48.463
Use only settings and televisions you are authorized to manage.

00:07:49.667 --> 00:07:56.285
For Vizio, use the pairing information requested by the television and wait for authentication.

00:07:56.285 --> 00:07:58.933
Check each operation on the TV screen.

00:07:58.933 --> 00:08:03.810
Do not assume every app, input, or button is available on every model.

00:08:05.033 --> 00:08:11.584
Roku uses its local network-control interface and does not require an invented pairing PIN.

00:08:11.584 --> 00:08:15.039
Enable network control where the TV requires it.

00:08:15.039 --> 00:08:21.014
GlintBeam still needs to verify the device before treating the connection as ready.

00:08:22.233 --> 00:08:28.474
Native Android and Google TV remote pairing is not available in this GlintBeam version.

00:08:28.474 --> 00:08:33.782
The presence of a brand-guide entry does not make that protocol supported.

00:08:33.782 --> 00:08:37.799
Some Sony TVs may use the separate Sony IP Control path.

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:44.789
Scroll through the selected Brand Guide for its preparation checklist and capability notes.

00:08:44.789 --> 00:08:48.033
If a connection fails, review these settings first.

00:08:48.033 --> 00:08:52.931
Only change television settings you understand and have permission to change.

00:08:54.133 --> 00:08:59.884
Privacy and Info is available at the top of the app, including during setup.

00:08:59.884 --> 00:09:07.376
Read how local profiles, TV requests, optional speech processing, and support messages are handled.

00:09:07.376 --> 00:09:10.932
Microphone audio is not received by AILoopLabs.

00:09:12.133 --> 00:09:17.817
The Usage tab explains network risks, TV compatibility, and third-party charges.

00:09:17.817 --> 00:09:23.643
GlintBeam itself has no account, advertising, or in-app purchases in this version.

00:09:23.643 --> 00:09:28.119
Television services may still have their own charges and terms.

00:09:29.333 --> 00:09:32.507
The Licenses tab lists software and font notices.

00:09:32.507 --> 00:09:36.134
For help, use the support link on the GlintBeam website.

00:09:36.134 --> 00:09:42.740
You can replay any chapter, read the written guide, or return to the quick start whenever you need it.

